{
  "id": "20261101-181719-662f",
  "hypothesis": "Raising ubatch_size from 512 to 1024 (batch_size stays 2048, FA=1, f16 KV) changes prefill throughput only where a prompt spans more than one ubatch, and grows peak VRAM by the size increase of the CUDA compute buffer. Predicted effects (estimates, not measurements): (a) pp512 is unchanged within noise. 512 tokens already fit in one ubatch at ub=512, so the graph, kernels and launch count are the same; any shift would come only from the different reserved buffer layout. (b) pp2048 drops from 4 ubatches to 2. Expected direction: a small gain, likely under 3%. Exp 20261101-180922-4bd0 indicated that prefill cost here is mostly per-token, and MMQ on Pascal (dp4a, no tensor cores) tiles over the token dimension in fixed-width column blocks, so weight re-reads scale with tokens more than with ubatch count. What a larger ubatch could save is per-ubatch fixed overhead (about 28 layers \u00d7 a few dozen kernel launches) plus some FA tile-kernel efficiency from more Q rows per KV pass. A null result is plausible and would itself show that ubatch count is not a prefill lever on this card. (c) tg128 is unchanged within noise, because decode runs one token per ubatch. (d) TTFT tracks whichever pp case matches the TTFT prompt length; if that prompt is 512 tokens or fewer, it is unchanged. (e) vram_peak_mib rises. The compute buffer scales roughly linearly with ubatch: FFN intermediates (ub \u00d7 8192), attention activations, and possibly an output/logits buffer of ub \u00d7 128256 \u00d7 4 B if the worst-case reserve assumes all outputs. Plausible range: +30 to +300 MiB. The measured delta estimates the ub=512 compute buffer size and decomposes part of the ~2.3 GB non-KV peak that exp 20261101-180922-4bd0 could not attribute. (f) KLD/PPL are unchanged, because ubatch does not alter the math beyond reduction-order effects. Note that the quality run uses -c 512, so it never exercises a 1024 ubatch.",
  "research_objective": "Isolate the effect of ubatch_size on pp2048/TTFT and measure the ubatch-dependent share of peak VRAM, on the promoted FA=1 f16-KV config.",
  "description": "Single-variable change: runtime.ubatch_size 512 -> 1024. Everything else is held at the promoted config: CUDA backend, commit 7bd18083 (b12021), no patches, no cmake flags, n_gpu_layers 99, flash_attn 1, f16/f16 KV, batch_size 2048, mmap 1, empty env. Interpretation plan: if pp2048 does not improve significantly, ubatch increases are closed as a throughput lever, and the VRAM delta tells us whether ub=256 is worth testing as a VRAM-saving option for the capacity profile. If pp2048 improves, the size of the gain against the VRAM cost decides whether ub=2048 is worth a follow-up.",
